There are 2 common types in databases: relational and non-relational
Relational:
  Data is stored in tabular format. Tabular format is systematic arrangement of rows and columns. 
  MS SQL, MySQL

Non-relational:
  Data is stored in key-value pairs.
  Commonly used: MongoDB, Amazon DynamoDB, Redis

